,"gloss":"doubt particle"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"lament particle"}],"gloss":"indeed?"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இரும்பல்","parts":[{"text":"இரும்பல்","lemma":"இரும்பல்","gloss":"dark and thick"}],"gloss":"dark and thick","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கூந்தல்","parts":[{"text":"கூந்தல்","lemma":"kūntal","gloss":"tresses"}],"gloss":"tresses"},{"surface":"மடந்தையர்","parts":[{"text":"மடந்தை","lemma":"maṭantai","gloss":"young woman"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"ar","gloss":"plural suffix"}],"gloss":"young women's"},{"surface":"தந்தை","parts":[{"text":"தந்தை","lemma":"tantai","gloss":"father"}],"gloss":"father"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடு","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"āṭu","gloss":"swaying"}],"gloss":"swaying"},{"surface":"கழை","parts":[{"text":"கழை","lemma":"kaḻai","gloss":"bamboo"}],"gloss":"bamboo"},{"surface":"நரலும்","parts":[{"text":"நரலும்","lemma":"naral","gloss":"sounding"}],"gloss":"sounding"},{"surface":"சேட்","parts":[{"text":"சேட்","lemma":"சேட்","gloss":"distant"}],"gloss":"distant","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சிமைப்","parts":[{"text":"சிமைப்","lemma":"சிமைப்","gloss":"peak's"}],"gloss":"peak's","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புலவர்","parts":[{"text":"புலவர்","lemma":"pulavar","gloss":"poet"}],"gloss":"poets"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடி","parts":[{"text":"பாடி","lemma":"pāṭi","gloss":"having sung"}],"gloss":"having sung"},{"surface":"யானாப்","parts":[{"text":"யானாப்","lemma":"யானாப்","gloss":"insatiably"}],"gloss":"insatiably","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பண்பிற்","parts":[{"text":"பண்பிற்","lemma":"பண்பிற்","gloss":"of noble character"}],"gloss":"of noble character","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பகைவர்","parts":[{"text":"பகைவர்","lemma":"pakaivar","gloss":"enemies"}],"gloss":"enemies"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஓடுகழல்","parts":[{"text":"ஓடு","lemma":"ōṭu","gloss":"fleeing"},{"text":"கழல்","lemma":"kaḻal","gloss":"warrior anklet"}],"gloss":"fleeing with warrior anklets"},{"surface":"கம்பலை","parts":[{"text":"கம்பலை","lemma":"kampalai","gloss":"uproar"}],"gloss":"uproar"},{"surface":"கண்ட","parts":[{"text":"கண்ட","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"who saw"}],"gloss":"who saw"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செருவெஞ்","parts":[{"text":"செருவெஞ்","lemma":"செருவெஞ்","gloss":"fierce in battle"}],"gloss":"fierce in battle","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சேஎய்","parts":[{"text":"சேஎய்","lemma":"சேஎய்","gloss":"Murugan-like"}],"gloss":"Murugan-like","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பெருவிறல்","parts":[{"text":"பெருமை","lemma":"perumai","gloss":"great"},{"text":"விறல்","lemma":"viṟal","gloss":"victory"}],"gloss":"greatly victorious"},{"surface":"நாடே","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"nāṭu","gloss":"land"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"land indeed"}]}],"literal":"In the heat-filled, matured Kino tree's red high ground, / with the moisture of the great downpour that sprouted in the rainy season, / so that the dry soil is mixed, having ploughed many times and sown, / at the fit season when many branches where lizards played, / because of weeding the roots, the leaf-sheaths grew thick and flourished, / resembling the young female peacock that has recently given birth, growing tall, / the black stems shot up, and together the young ears of grain opened, / below and above, without leaving any part, bearing many fruits, / to harvest the beautifully matured new varagu millet, / while foxtail millet is harvested, and the pods of hyacinth beans turn dark, / the pale pods of the lush vines reaching the stage of being gathered, / the clarified liquor of toddy matured by being buried in the ground, / distributing to every house of the grass-thatched huts, / cooking rice by sizzling chickpeas in fragrant ghee, / so that the bustle of eating plates on great shoulders occurs, / will it still flourish with effortless fresh fertility? / The father of the young women with dark, thick tresses, / on the distant peaks where swaying bamboos whistle, whom poets / sing of without end, he of noble character, who saw / the distressed uproar of enemies fleeing with their anklets, / that fierce-in-battle Murugan-like hero's great victorious land!","translation":"Will it still flourish with effortless, fresh abundance—the great, victorious land of the fierce-in-battle, Murugan-like hero, the father of young women with thick, dark tresses? He was of such noble character that poets never ceased singing of him on his high peaks where swaying bamboos whistle, and he witnessed the distressed uproar of enemies fleeing with their warrior anklets. In that land, on the red high ground where Kino trees grow in the heat, after the great downpour of the rainy season brought moisture, they ploughed many times to mix the dry soil and sowed seeds. In the season when lizards play on many branches, they weeded the roots, and the leaf-sheaths grew thick and flourished. Resembling a young peahen that has recently laid eggs, the black stems shot up, and the young ears of grain opened together, bearing fruit abundantly below and above without fail. As they harvested the beautifully matured new varagu millet, plucked the foxtail millet, and the pods of the lush hyacinth bean vines turned dark and reached the stage of gathering, they distributed clarified toddy matured by being buried in the ground to every grass-thatched hut, and cooked rice by sizzling chickpeas in fragrant ghee, making a joyful bustle of plates on their strong shoulders.","modern":"கரிய அடர்ந்த கூந்தலையுடைய மகளிரின் தந்தையும், அசையும் மூங்கில்கள் ஒலிக்கும் உயர்ந்த மலை உச்சியை உடையவனும், புலவர்கள் பாடித் தீராத பண்பாளனும், போர்க்களத்தில் பகைவர்கள் தம் வீரக்கழல்கள் ஒலிக்க அஞ்சி ஓடும் ஆரவாரத்தைக் கண்டவனுமாகிய, போர் விரும்பும் முருகன் போன்ற பேராற்றல் கொண்ட பாரியின் நாடு இனிமேலும் இத்தகைய வருத்தமில்லாத புதிய வளத்தோடு செழித்திருக்குமோ? வெப்பம் நிறைந்த வேங்கை மரங்கள் உள்ள சிவந்த மேட்டு நிலத்தில், கார்ப்பருவத்து மழையினால் உண்டான ஈரப்பதம் கொண்டு, புழுதி மண்ணைக் கலந்து பலமுறை உழுது விதைத்தனர். பல்லிகள் விளையாடும் கிளைகளையுடைய செவ்விய காலத்தில், களைகளை வேரோடு களைந்ததால் பயிர்கள் தழைத்து வளர்ந்தன. அண்மையில் முட்டையிட்ட மென்மையான பெண் மயிலைப் போலப் பயிர்கள் நீண்டு வளர்ந்து, கரிய தாள்கள் ஓங்கி, கதிர்கள் ஒருசேர விரிந்து, கீழும் மேலும் குறையின்றிக் காய்த்தன. அவ்வாறு அழகாக விளைந்த புதிய வரகினை அறுக்கவும், தினையைக் கொய்யவும், அவரைக்கொடியின் வெளுத்த காய்கள் முற்றிப் பறிக்கும் பக்குவத்தை அடையவும், நிலத்தில் புதைத்து வைத்துப் பக்குவப்படுத்திய தெளிந்த கள்ளினைப் புல்லால் வேய்ந்த குடில்கள் தோறும் பகிர்ந்து கொடுத்து, நறிய நெய்யில் கடலையைத் தாளித்துச் சோறாக்கி, பெரிய தோள்களையுடைய மக்கள் உண்கலங்களின் ஒலியோடு மகிழ்ந்துண்ணும் இத்தகைய வளமான நாடு இனிப் பொலிவிழந்து போகுமோ?","explanation":"The poet Kapilar laments the death of his close friend and patron, King Vēḷ Pāri, after his Parampu hills were besieged and taken. He looks at the land, which was once incredibly fertile and self-sufficient, and wonders if it will ever retain its effortless prosperity now that its protector is gone. The poem beautifully describes the agricultural cycle of the Parampu hills, where millets and beans grow abundantly and the people share aged toddy and rich food in every thatched hut. This vivid picture of peaceful, abundant life contrasts sharply with the tragic loss of the king, highlighting the grief of the poet.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.26,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.2],[1.2,1.6],[1.6,1.8],[1.8,2.7],[2.7,2.9],[2.9,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,3.86],[3.86,4.3],[4.3,4.7],[4.7,5.49],[5.49,5.8],[5.8,6.0],[6.0,6.4],[6.4,7.4],[7.4,7.84],[7.84,8.56],[8.56,8.91],[8.91,9.09],[9.26,9.44],[9.62,9.79],[9.79,10.5],[10.5,10.97],[10.97,11.2],[11.2,12.4],[12.4,12.6],[12.6,12.8],[12.8,13.2],[13.2,13.5],[13.5,13.9],[13.9,14.83],[14.83,15.2],[15.2,15.7],[15.7,16.1],[16.1,16.5],[16.5,17.6],[17.6,18.1],[18.1,18.75],[18.75,18.9],[18.9,19.2],[20.04,20.64],[20.64,20.97],[20.97,21.14],[21.14,21.44],[21.44,21.84],[22.57,22.76],[22.76,23.15],[23.15,23.44],[23.44,23.74],[23.74,24.53],[24.53,25.34],[25.34,25.87],[25.87,26.06],[26.06,26.